<title>UK: Commercial Union up on positive comment.</title>
<headline>Commercial Union up on positive comment.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British insurer Commercial Union Plc held their early gains by midday Thursday as BZW repeated a &quot;buy&quot; on the stock and SBC Warburg moved its rating to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;take profits,&quot; traders said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 12-1/2p at 678-1/2 by 1234 GMT in volume of 2.3 million shares, after on Wednesday dropping to its lowest level in over two months.</p>
<p>Sources said BZW had set a price target of 814p on the stock but analysts at SBC Warburg declined comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
